### 克1 | _Hak(7)_ [[hak1]]

$$
R
  ⼉ + 5
U
  U+514B
A
  ==
  - 剋
  - 勀
  - 勊
  - 尅
  ==
V
  ==
  - haak1 (longer syllable)
  ==
F
  ==
  - (F2.33 克) ::[能]也勝也又聚斂曰[掊]克::
  ==
W
  ====
  - [[Page~69 克(7)]]
    ==
    - To sustain``, to carry`` [[Kangxi: 肩也]], adequate to [[Kangxi: 肩任也任者又負荷之名也能勝此物謂之克也, 克能也]];
    - superior to;
    - to subdue, to conquer [[Kangxi: 勝也]];
    - overbearing;
    - _hak(7) chai(3)_
        [[hak1 zai3 克制]]
        to order, to make one obey;
    - _hak(7) (2)f(u/)_
        [[hak1 fu2 克苦]],
        hurried, oppressed;
    - _fat(7) hak(7) (1)shing yam(6)_
        [[fat1 hak1 sing1 jam6 弗克勝任]]
        inadequate for the place;
    - _hak(7) (1)tong_
        [[hak1 dong1 克當]],
        to sustain, fit for;
    - _hak(7) (2)k(i/)_
        [[hak1 gei2 克己]],
        to do what you ask others, self-government.
    ==
  ====
C
  ==
  - Fan Wan entry: Fixed missing stroke in 能 and corrected 拮 to 掊.
  - Williams' "to subdue, to conquer": This requires Kangxi 勝也
    to be departing-tone.
  - Williams' 克制: In modern usage, a reflexive "restrain"
    rather than a transitive "subdue".
  ==
P
  ++
  1. To subdue (oneself), to restrain (Kangxi: 勝己之私謂之克).
  ++
L
  ====
  * 【克】 (khok)
    ==
    - (_verb-like_) [to] sustain, [to] carry
    - (_adjective-like_) capable
    - (_verb-like_) [to] overcome, [to] vanquish
    - (_verb-like_) [to] subdue
    ==
  ====
$$

### 黑1 | _Hak(7)_ [[hak1]]

$$
R
  ⿊ + 0
U
  U+9ED1
V
  ==
  - haak1 (longer syllable)
  ==
F
  ==
  - (F2.33 黑) 北方之色
  ==
W
  ====
  - [[Page~69 黑(7)]]
    ==
    - Black [[Kangxi: 火所熏之色也, 北方隂色]], sooty;
    - dark, obscure [[Kangxi: 黑晦也如晦冥時色也]];
    - cloudy, dull;
    - wicked;
    - _hak(7) shik(7)_
        [[hak1 sik1 黑色]]
        black color;
    - _hak(7) (o\)m(3)_
        [[hak1 am3 黑暗]]
        dark, not well lighted;
    - _hak(7) (1)sam_
        [[hak1 sam1 黑心]],
        villainous;
    - _hak(7) fo(3)_
        [[hak1 fo3 黑貨]]
        opium;
    - _hak(7) p(a/)k(9) (4)n(a/)n (1)fan_
        [[hak1 baak6 naan4 fan1 黑白難分]],
        good and bad are not easily distinguished;
    - _(1)kam (5)m(a/)n hak(7)_
        [[gam1 maan5-1 hak1 今晚黑]]
        to-night.
    ==
  ====
C
  ==
  - Williams' 黑貨: More generally, contraband.
  ==
P
  ++
  1. The 203rd~radical (U+2FCA ⿊ "black").
  ++
L
  ====
  * 【黑】 (xok)
    ==
    - (_adjective-like_) black
    ==
  ====
E
  ====
  - 【黑麻麻】 (hak1 maa4-1 maa4-1)
    ++
    1. Very dark (of viewing conditions).
    ++
  - 【黑{𠵼=⿰口孟}{𠵼=⿰口孟}】 (hak1 mang1 mang1)
    ++
    1. Very dark (of viewing conditions, or in colour).
    ++
  - 【黑咪{𠵼=⿰口孟}】 (hak1 mi1 mang1)
    ++
    1. Synonym of [黑{𠵼=⿰口孟}{𠵼=⿰口孟}](#cantonese-黑𠵼𠵼).
    ++
  - 【黑屎竻掘】 (hak1 si2 lak6 gwak6)
    ++
    1. Black or very dark in colour (when undesirable).
    ++
  ====
  --
  The spellings
    {𠵼=⿰口孟}{𠵼=⿰口孟} for mang1 mang1,
    咪{𠵼=⿰口孟} for mi1 mang1, and
    竻掘 for lak6 gwak6
   are arbitrary;
  these are likely phonetic suffixes.
  --
